{"name":"Poetry Reading","hex":"#9faec9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"poetry reading","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A public oral recitation or performance of poetry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poetry_reading"}],"entries":[{"title":"Poetry reading","blocks":[{"text":"A poetry reading is a public oral recitation or performance of poetry. Reading poetry aloud allows the reader to express their own experience through poetry, changing the poem according to their sensibilities. The reader uses pitch and stress, and pauses become apparent. A poetry reading typically takes place on a small stage in a café or bookstore where multiple poets recite their own work. A more prominent poet may be chosen as the \"headliner\" of such an event and famous poets may also take the stage at a bigger venue such as an amphitheater or college auditorium."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Kyle_Dacuyan_at_the_Poesiefestival_Berlin_2019_03.jpg/330px-Kyle_Dacuyan_at_the_Poesiefestival_Berlin_2019_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poetry_reading","wikidata":"Q7207537"},{"title":"Poetry","blocks":[{"text":"Poetry is a form of literary art that uses aesthetic and often rhythmic qualities of language to evoke meanings in addition to, or in place of, literal or surface-level meanings. A particular instance of poetry is a poem and is written by a poet. Poets use a variety of techniques called poetic devices, such as assonance, alliteration, consonance, euphony and cacophony, onomatopoeia, rhythm, rhyme schemes and sound symbolism, to produce musical or other artistic effects. They also frequently organize these devices into poetic structures, which may be strict or loose, conventional or invented by the poet. Poetic structures vary dramatically by language and cultural convention, but they often rely on rhythmic metre: patterns of syllable stress or syllable weight. They may also use repeating patterns of phonemes, phoneme groups, tones, words, or entire phrases. Poetic structures may even be semantic."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poetry","wikidata":"Q482"},{"title":"Reading","blocks":[{"text":"Reading is the process of taking in the sense or meaning of the symbols of a written language, by means of sight or touch.\nThe ability to read is called literacy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Muse_reading_Louvre_CA2220_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Muse_reading_Louvre_CA2220_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reading","wikidata":"Q199657"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Charles_Simic_reading.jpg/500px-Charles_Simic_reading.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Charles_Simic_reading.jpg/1280px-Charles_Simic_reading.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Charles_Simic_reading.jpg/500px-Charles_Simic_reading.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Charles Simic reading at Shakespeare & Co. (Paris, France) on July 11, 2013.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharles_Simic_reading.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Marian_Palla_v_roce_2022.jpg/500px-Marian_Palla_v_roce_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Marian_Palla_v_roce_2022.jpg/1280px-Marian_Palla_v_roce_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Marian_Palla_v_roce_2022.